cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this release of the software and the accompanying paper, Resolving Tusnády's Problem."
type: software
title: "Tusnády's problem in Lean 4"
authors:
  - family-names: Wengiel
    given-names: Nicola
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics, FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicolawengiel/tusnady-lean"
url: "https://github.com/nicolawengiel/tusnady-lean/releases/tag/v0.2.0"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of the sharp worst-case combinatorial discrepancy
  bounds for closed lower orthants and closed bounded axis-parallel boxes
  in every fixed dimension d ≥ 2. The proof combines Nicola Wengiel's
  higher-dimensional lower bound, Zhewei Wei's planar lower bound and
  Aleksandar Nikolov's matching upper bound. The constants are independent
  of the number of points. Wei's reused planar proof retains its MIT license.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formalized mathematics
  - discrepancy theory
  - Tusnády's problem
